00:04:34.921 --> 00:04:36.729
- Oops.

00:04:36.729 --> 00:04:40.170
(bomb explodes)

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:42.690
- Okay, let's back up and
talk about that very first

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:44.360
nuclear test in New Mexico.

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:45.730
This is the bomb that they used.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:46.850
They blew this thing up

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.020
in the most remote place they could find

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.760
in the U.S., 100 miles
south of Albuquerque

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.470
in the middle of the New Mexican desert.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:55.180
Because this was the first nuke ever,

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:56.970
no one really knew what was gonna happen.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.180
They had no idea how
explosive this thing was.

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:01.270
And so this guy who ran the test range,

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:02.640
his name was Norris Bradbury,

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:05.700
he was in charge of measuring this,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.120
of assessing how big the blast was

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:09.377
so he could report and be like,

00:05:09.377 --> 00:05:11.130
"These nuclear bombs are this powerful."

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:13.521
He was not ready for what he saw next.

00:05:13.521 --> 00:05:15.380
(bomb explodes)

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:18.837
After the explosion, he
said, verbatim, quote,

00:05:18.837 --> 00:05:22.337
"The atom bomb did not fit
into any preconceptions

00:05:22.337 --> 00:05:25.240
"possessed by anybody",
i.e. you can't fathom

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.260
how insanely powerful this thing is.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.700
You could see the flash

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:32.080
and feel the shockwave
from 160 miles away.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.530
It was clear that this
bomb was unpredictable

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:35.630
and hard to measure,

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:37.520
and scientists were
realizing that the radiation

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.300
from this bomb could spread
and they didn't know how much

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.810
and how far and how dangerous
this thing would be.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:44.670
The director of the project
of the nuclear weapons

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.030
sort of freaked out with
the lack of precision

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:47.863
on all of this.

00:05:47.863 --> 00:05:49.067
He's like, "Did we just poison

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:52.094
"the entire Southwestern
United States with radiation?"

00:05:52.094 --> 00:05:53.510
(suspenseful music)

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:56.500
So they realized that they had
to find a more remote place

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.330
if they were gonna keep
testing their nukes.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.920
And so this is where the treasure hunt

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:02.840
for the perfect nuclear
testing site begins.

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.090
- It is the duty of the military services

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:07.740
to explore the military
might of this new weapon.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.070
- So you get these two Naval
officers who were tasked

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.410
with finding the next nuclear test site,

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:13.907
and they literally just said, quote,

00:06:13.907 --> 00:06:15.617
"We just took out a dozen maps

00:06:15.617 --> 00:06:18.560
"and started looking for remote sites."

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:20.020
Okay, I can get on board
with just pulling out

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.050
a bunch of maps and just perusing around,

00:06:22.050 --> 00:06:23.820
it's sort of what I do in my spare time

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.460
so I can totally see this happening.

00:06:25.460 --> 00:06:26.610
As they were looking at these maps,

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.930
they quickly realized
that nowhere in the U.S.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:31.690
is a good fit for a nuclear test site.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.190
They needed somewhere that
was extremely far away

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.620
from population centers

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.540
and they needed it to
be not freezing cold,

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:39.580
like in Alaska or something.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.250
I'm just imagining Harry Truman,
the president at the time.

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.180
In the course of 30 days,

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:48.410
this guy just tested this
new bonkers technology,

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:51.650
which happened to put
an entire city at risk.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:55.030
He literally destroyed two Japanese cities

00:06:55.030 --> 00:06:57.350
and won the war with this technology.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:00.210
From a global control and
leadership perspective,

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:03.270
this guy is feeling very powerful,

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.100
except for he's a little bit nervous

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.150
about the intel that the USSR

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.200
is working on the same weapon.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.610
They've been doing it for three years,

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.400
and the world is generally
in a state of uncertainty.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:16.470
Empires that ruled for
centuries are losing control.

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.710
There's now two governments
that are competing

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:20.740
for global dominance, and these weapons,

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.300
these nuclear weapons,
are the key to winning.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:24.770
And now Truman is being told

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:27.310
that you can't test these
weapons on American soil

00:07:27.310 --> 00:07:29.480
because they're too close
to population centers.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:30.780
So what do you do?

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:33.840
So Truman decides that if
the perfect nuclear test site

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:37.180
doesn't exist, he will make it exist.

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:38.460
So back to these maps.

00:07:38.460 --> 00:07:39.293
Where do we go?

00:07:39.293 --> 00:07:40.540
Where do we set up the test site?

00:07:40.540 --> 00:07:44.450
They start looking far
far away off of U.S. soil,

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:46.610
deep into the ocean, and
they eventually settled

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:50.750
on this little strip of beach
called the Bikini Atoll.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:52.640
- [Man] This is Bikini.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.398
It is here that the military
and scientific personnel

00:07:55.398 --> 00:07:57.473
conduct the tests for the atomic bomb.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.420
- The name Bikini means coconut island

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:03.160
roughly in the local language.

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.410
They liked this island
because the weather was good.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:07.860
There wasn't a lot of storms
and it had this nice lagoon

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.210
that they could position
a Naval fleet there

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.420
to see what nuclear weapons
do to Naval vessels.

00:08:13.420 --> 00:08:15.830
These islands had sort of
been conquered by Japan,

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:18.110
but then the U.S.
obviously conquered Japan

00:08:18.110 --> 00:08:19.950
so they sort of took over these islands,

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:22.860
but they didn't officially
own them, but they wanted to.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:25.020
The problem was that there
was a bunch of people

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.560
living on these islands.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.850
Oh, and by the way, this isn't 1893.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:31.240
You can just show up and
steal islands anymore

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:33.220
without people getting sort of pissed off.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.710
So Harry Truman, what do you do?

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:36.630
You send in this guy.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:38.157
- Mr. Ben Wyatt.

00:08:38.157 --> 00:08:39.240
- Thank you, thanks.

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:41.048
- The guy's name was Ben Wyatt.

00:08:41.048 --> 00:08:42.470
No, no, no, no, not, not that one.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:44.723
It's a different one from the 40s,

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:49.560
and he is on a mission to obtain
this Atoll from the locals

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.950
so that the U.S. can turn it
into their nuclear playground.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:55.980
One of the secret reasons why
the U.S. picked this island

00:08:55.980 --> 00:08:57.830
wasn't just because of the
weather and the lagoon,

00:08:57.830 --> 00:09:01.320
it was also because these
people had already been visited

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:02.910
by Christian missionaries.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:06.350
They were used to white people
arriving to their country

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:08.400
and trying to convince them of things,

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.940
and this became really useful.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.810
So one Sunday after church,

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:15.240
he gathers all the local Bikinians

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:18.340
to ask them if they would
like to leave their island,

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:19.173
and he promises them,

00:09:19.173 --> 00:09:20.157
"This will be temporary.

00:09:20.157 --> 00:09:21.790
"We just need it for a little bit."

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.930
And people are like, "Okay."

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.900
But don't worry, Ben is prepared for this.

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:27.320
He's got something in his back pocket.

00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.120
He starts to compare the Bikinians

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:33.130
to the children of
Israel, the chosen people,

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:35.960
saying that this is their
duty to leave the islands

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:39.110
so that the U.S. can
pursue their noble aim

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:41.190
of testing nuclear weapons.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:42.800
- [Newscaster] The
United States government

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:47.180
now wants to turn this
great destructive power

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:50.810
into something for the benefit of mankind.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:53.210
- He's just buttering them up with Jesus,

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:54.737
and it is so blatant.

00:09:54.737 --> 00:09:58.300
- Everything being in God's
hands, it must be good.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:01.260
- So eventually, we're not
really sure how it all went down

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:04.380
with whatever backroom deals,
but under the condition

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:05.917
that these people would
be able to come back,

00:10:05.917 --> 00:10:08.410
they agreed to leave the island,

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:10.147
to hand them over to the U.S.

00:10:10.147 --> 00:10:12.640
"But wait, don't go yet", says Ben Wyatt.

00:10:12.640 --> 00:10:15.610
After the deal is made,
he invites a film crew

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:19.150
from National Geographic
to stage a reenactment

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:22.540
of the whole scenario to
make a film for a month.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:25.310
- Crossroads scene 25, take one.

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:27.640
- They had these shoots in the churches

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:28.736
that they had to have the people there

00:10:28.736 --> 00:10:30.590
go to church several times

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:32.219
so that they could get
it from different angles.

00:10:32.219 --> 00:10:33.797
- [Narrator] First they
sing their own version

00:10:33.797 --> 00:10:36.190
of "Glory to God in the Highest."

00:10:36.190 --> 00:10:39.857
(speaking foreign language)

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:48.010
- They made this huge propaganda film

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:49.070
and guess who it was for?

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:50.000
The American people.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.577
It was like, "Look, United States,

00:10:51.577 --> 00:10:53.257
"yes we're taking over this island,

00:10:53.257 --> 00:10:54.927
"but look at how happy these people are.

00:10:54.927 --> 00:10:55.867
"They love this.

00:10:55.867 --> 00:10:57.437
"Look at how cool Ben Wyatt is

00:10:57.437 --> 00:11:02.340
"with his charismatic, convincing,
persuasive Jesus talk."

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:03.700
So the U.S. is one step closer

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:05.350
to having their nuclear playground.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.949
They ship away these
natives to nearby islands

00:11:07.949 --> 00:11:10.573
with no food, water or shelter,

00:11:15.739 --> 00:11:18.049
and then the bombs begin.

00:11:18.049 --> 00:11:22.049
- [Announcer] It is now
30 seconds to zero time.

00:11:24.119 --> 00:11:26.786
(bomb explodes)

00:11:28.190 --> 00:11:30.640
They dropped their first
nuke on the Bikini Atoll

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:33.370
on June 30th, 1946.

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:36.630
These were much bigger bombs
than were dropped in Japan,

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.210
and unlike the original
tests, which were very secret,

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:41.360
the U.S. now wanted the world,

00:11:41.360 --> 00:11:43.910
or the Soviet Union, to know about it.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:47.560
It was like a giant PR campaign,
the opposite of top secret.

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:49.498
- [Radio Announcer] The radio
station will be broadcasting

00:11:49.498 --> 00:11:51.640
from Bikini.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:52.530
- And it totally worked.

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:53.857
Soon the whole world was like,

00:11:53.857 --> 00:11:54.690
"What?

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.277
"The U.S. is testing atomic bombs

00:11:57.277 --> 00:11:59.410
"on a random atoll in the
middle of the Pacific?

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:02.200
A few days after this
first test on Bikini,

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:06.180
a French fashion designer
released his new swimsuit.

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:09.970
It was a two-piece women's
swimsuit that, wait for it,

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:12.210
revealed a woman's belly button.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:13.330
Highly scandalous.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.770
There was a ton of outcry,
it was highly controversial,

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:17.810
and when he announced
it, he saw an opportunity

00:12:17.810 --> 00:12:20.500
to ride this publicity wave happening

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.620
from the nuclear tests,

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:24.259
so he named this swimsuit the bikini.

00:12:24.259 --> 00:12:26.842
(groovy music)

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:33.710
It was radical, it was
scandalous, it was controversial,

00:12:33.710 --> 00:12:35.680
but it totally worked.

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:39.170
- The question: should bikinis be banned?

00:12:39.170 --> 00:12:41.860
- He and his swimsuit
got tons of attention,

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:43.230
both good and bad.

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:45.430
- Do you think bikinis should be banned?

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:47.110
- Well, I most certainly do.

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:48.372
- No, definitely not, no.

00:12:48.372 --> 00:12:51.790
- Rather than wear a bikini,
why wear anything at all?

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:54.630
- But the naming of the
bikini is just the beginning

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:57.260
of how these nuclear bombs started shaping

00:12:57.260 --> 00:12:59.443
and influencing popular culture.

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:06.380
Children's toys, comics,
cartoons, superheroes,

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:09.360
alcoholic drinks, beauty pageants, songs.

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:11.810
The word atomic was everywhere.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:14.830
People started saying, "You're
the bomb" as a compliment.

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:17.910
People calling someone
"Atomic" now meant you're hot.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:19.910
And all the while, the tests on Bikini

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:21.840
got bigger and more frequent,

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:25.180
way way bigger than anything
that happened in Japan.

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:28.270
You know, that bomb that
killed over 350,000 people.

00:13:28.270 --> 00:13:29.960
Yeah, these bombs were way bigger

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:31.490
and people started to get scared,

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:34.860
so much show that the commander
for these Bikini tests

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:37.150
had to get up in front of the nation

00:13:37.150 --> 00:13:39.200
and dispel some of these fears,

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:42.170
like whether or not the bomb
would blow up the whole ocean.

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.680
- The bomb will not start a
chain reaction in the water.

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:47.730
- Or whether or not it would
turn the ocean into gas.

00:13:47.730 --> 00:13:51.050
- Converting it all to
gas, letting all the ships

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:52.767
on all the oceans drop down to the bottom.

00:13:52.767 --> 00:13:54.570
- One of the leading theories

00:13:54.570 --> 00:13:56.660
was that this bomb was so intense

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:57.880
that it would crack open the Earth

00:13:57.880 --> 00:13:59.340
and the core would leak out,

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:01.170
and it would be the end of gravity.

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:03.280
- It will not blow out
the bottom of the sea

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.820
and let all the water run down the hole.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.210
It will not destroy gravity.

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:10.300
I am not an atomic Playboy.

00:14:10.300 --> 00:14:12.960
- Wait, what, what did she just say?

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:14.803
- I am not an atomic Playboy.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:17.864
- Oh my God.

00:14:17.864 --> 00:14:19.590
(Johnny laughing)

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:22.240
So it turns out this guy was in love

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:23.850
with what was happening on Bikini.

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:25.560
He was just so into this.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:29.670
And after the first test, he
staged a giant celebration,

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:33.990
in which a literal nuke
shaped cake was produced.

00:14:33.990 --> 00:14:35.560
And it turns out that some
people didn't like the fact

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:38.520
that this guy was celebrating the advent

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.540
of this destructive weapon,

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:43.017
especially surrounded by women, quote,

00:14:43.017 --> 00:14:44.680
"Dressed to the nines."

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:46.540
And so, because of all of this partying

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:49.880
and the cake and whatever, he
was dubbed the atomic Playboy,

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.460
which is just an amazing title.

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:54.150
- I am not an atomic Playboy.

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.770
- Okay, but there's one
more very important way

00:14:56.770 --> 00:15:00.580
that these nuclear tests on
Bikini influenced our culture,

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:03.810
and it's not swimsuits,
and it's not even SpongeBob

00:15:03.810 --> 00:15:05.810
who lives in Bikini Bottom

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:07.720
and occasionally has a run-in with nukes.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.063
- Atom by atom!

00:15:12.272 --> 00:15:13.122
Uh oh.

00:15:13.122 --> 00:15:15.140
(bombs exploding)

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.420
- It's what happened in February 1954,

00:15:18.420 --> 00:15:22.860
when they tested this guy,
a particularly huge bomb,

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:25.700
a thousand times larger than Hiroshima.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:27.490
When this bomb was detonated in Bikini,

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:31.620
a Japanese tuna fishing boat
named Lucky Dragon was nearby.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:32.660
I mean, it wasn't nearby,

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:35.260
but it, for this bomb, it was in range.

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:38.150
It received a large dose of radiation,

00:15:38.150 --> 00:15:41.250
and the crew of 23 men returned to Japan,

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.470
where they were hospitalized.

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:45.510
It was reported that some
of the tuna from their boat

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:48.250
was sold and consumed
by Japanese citizens.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:50.000
- [Newscaster] The
ship's cargo of tuna fish

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.690
was found to be radioactive

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.160
and had to be buried in the ground.

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:56.060
- You have to understand,
radiation is a freaky thing.

00:15:56.060 --> 00:16:00.440
It is this invisible force
that destroys your cells

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:03.580
without you ever seeing or
feeling anything at first.

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:04.630
This panic spread

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:07.470
and Japan's fishing
economy took a giant hit.

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:09.490
Japanese citizens were horrified.

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:11.890
- [Newscaster] Throughout the
towns and villages of Japan,

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:13.608
the people, young and old,

00:16:13.608 --> 00:16:16.910
are adding their
signatures to this appeal.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:20.150
Stop the experiments, outflow the bomb.

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:22.670
- And when activists
created a protest film,

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.800
which took place on an island

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:27.653
that has a very similar
resemblance to Bikini.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:33.240
And then near this island, a
monster named Gojira is born.

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:35.517
He comes out of the ocean, quote,

00:16:35.517 --> 00:16:38.900
"Emitting high levels
of H bomb radiation."

00:16:38.900 --> 00:16:40.300
Are you getting where we're going here?

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:42.070
The first thing that the monster does

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:45.300
after emerging was destroying a tuna boat

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.240
labeled Lucky Dragon.

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:48.500
I mean, this is totally on the nose.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:50.560
It's not a hidden symbolism film.

00:16:50.560 --> 00:16:54.230
This film was a pointed
protest at all of these tests

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:55.660
and the effects that they were having

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:58.760
on the local people,
ecology and economies.

00:16:58.760 --> 00:17:02.010
And it helped mobilize a
fierce anti-nuclear movement

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:03.900
in Japan that was already there

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:06.200
because of what Japan
had already experienced.

00:17:08.440 --> 00:17:11.010
Oh, and the film was actually pretty good.

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:12.810
So the film actually came to the U.S. too.

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:14.860
It was dubbed over in
English for U.S. audiences,

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:16.840
but it was renamed to Godzilla

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.720
and it was edited to remove

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:21.670
all of the overt anti-nuclear symbols.

00:17:21.670 --> 00:17:23.247
The government's like, "We
can't have that happening.

00:17:23.247 --> 00:17:25.567
"We're putting so much work into the PR

00:17:25.567 --> 00:17:27.987
"of projecting how good
nuclear weapons are.

00:17:27.987 --> 00:17:29.917
"No way some protest film from Japan

00:17:29.917 --> 00:17:32.160
"about a monster is gonna derail this."

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:35.120
So Godzilla lost its protest appeal

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:37.210
and became just another monster movie.

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:38.927
- [Announcer] Dynamic violence!

00:17:38.927 --> 00:17:40.276
Savage action!

00:17:40.276 --> 00:17:42.100
Spectacular thrills!

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:44.410
- In the years following World War two,

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:48.080
this is the total amount of
explosive force detonated

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:50.010
between the U.S. and Soviet Union.

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:52.260
But when broken down by location,

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:55.620
you can see that 87%
of this explosive force

00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:57.340
took place right here.

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.340
So many bombs were dropped here,

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.560
including one named Castle Bravo,

00:18:01.560 --> 00:18:04.940
which was literally a
thousand times more powerful

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:06.970
than the one dropped on Hiroshima.

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:08.700
There's no way we can fathom this really,

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.650
but we can sort of try
to do a thought exercise

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:12.730
to understand how
powerful these bombs are.

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:14.930
If you detonated this
here in Washington DC,

00:18:14.930 --> 00:18:19.930
90% of the population of DC
and Baltimore and Philadelphia

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:24.200
and New York would disappear
in just three days.

00:18:24.200 --> 00:18:27.240
Okay, so unsurprisingly, back in Bikini,

00:18:27.240 --> 00:18:28.840
the locals never got to go back.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:30.550
That was never the intention.

00:18:30.550 --> 00:18:31.580
It was all a lie,

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:34.060
as much of a lie as the
propaganda film itself.

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:36.460
Even if they did go back, it
would be a death sentence.

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:38.690
A recent study found that
this group of islands

00:18:38.690 --> 00:18:42.370
is more radioactive than the
Chernobyl exclusion zone.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:43.203
But guess what?

00:18:43.203 --> 00:18:44.036
No one cared.

00:18:44.036 --> 00:18:45.010
No one cares.

00:18:45.010 --> 00:18:48.190
When told about this
radioactivity in the Pacific,

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:51.097
Secretary of State Henry
Kissinger said, and I quote,

00:18:51.097 --> 00:18:53.847
"There are only 90,000 of them out there.

00:18:53.847 --> 00:18:55.000
"Who gives a damn?"

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:55.833
What an asshole.

00:18:55.833 --> 00:18:58.090
So this story explains how we got the name

00:18:58.090 --> 00:18:59.950
for the swimsuit, the bikini,

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:01.850
why SpongeBob lives where he lives

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:04.600
and why we use the word
bomb as a compliment.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:06.720
But it also teaches us a deeper lesson

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:09.730
about what lengths we
will go to retain power,

00:19:09.730 --> 00:19:12.630
or as some frame it, to maintain peace.

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:14.640
That's a complicated paradox to entangle,

00:19:14.640 --> 00:19:17.240
especially when this peace
that we're talking about

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:20.620
relies on the potential
of absolute destruction.

00:19:20.620 --> 00:19:23.630
The race to build and
test these nuclear weapons

00:19:23.630 --> 00:19:27.730
led to the U.S. not taking
the risk on their own soil.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:30.010
Instead, doing what we've done so expertly

00:19:30.010 --> 00:19:31.720
for many many decades,

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:34.970
exporting that risk and those consequences

00:19:34.970 --> 00:19:38.150
to faraway places, to places
where we can manipulate

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:42.073
and lie to the people and then
pollute their oceans forever.

